---
const faqs = [
  {
    question: "Do I need to know how to code?",
    answer:
      "No. You describe what you want and the agent does the editing. If you do code, the project is plain Astro and Tailwind, so you can open it in any editor.",
  },
  {
    question: "What is a change?",
    answer:
      "A change is a draft of your site. Edits in a change stay separate from the live site until you publish them, so you can try ideas without breaking anything.",
  },
  {
    question: "Where does my site live?",
    answer:
      "In a Git repository you own. When a change is ready, publish it from the app and it becomes the live site.",
  },
  {
    question: "Can I edit content without the agent?",
    answer:
      "Yes. Blog posts and help articles have friendly forms in the Content panel. The agent is there when you want bigger changes.",
  },
  {
    question: "Can I undo something?",
    answer:
      "Yes. Every save is a checkpoint, and History lets you restore any earlier version in one click.",
  },
];
---

<section class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-8 py-16" id="faq">
  <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-4xl">Frequently asked questions</h2>
  <div class="mt-8 space-y-3">
    {
      faqs.map((faq) => (
        <details class="group rounded-xl border border-neutral-200 p-5 transition-colors open:border-neutral-300 dark:border-neutral-800 dark:open:border-neutral-700">
          <summary class="cursor-pointer list-none font-semibold marker:hidden">
            <span class="flex items-center justify-between gap-4">
              {faq.question}
              <span class="text-neutral-400 transition-transform group-open:rotate-45 dark:text-neutral-500">+</span>
            </span>
          </summary>
          <p class="mt-3 text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400">{faq.answer}</p>
        </details>
      ))
    }
  </div>
</section>
